WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.025
Digital Asset Architect brings the whole toolkit together into a research process you can defend.

2
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:14.374
Start with a precise question and the exact identity of the asset: its id,

3
00:00:14.374 --> 00:00:16.062
network and contract.

4
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:22.413
Then gather sourced data, analyse supply, protocol economics, network activity,

5
00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:27.719
liquidity and risk, run scenarios, and write down what is unknown.

6
00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:32.217
Protocol data has its own vocabulary.

7
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:37.073
Total value locked is capital deposited, priced at market.

8
00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:39.083
Fees are what users pay.

9
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:43.102
Revenue is the share of fees the protocol keeps.

10
00:00:43.102 --> 00:00:47.624
None of them is a company’s audited revenue or profit.

11
00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:51.968
Decentralised finance moves risk around.

12
00:00:51.968 --> 00:01:02.864
A liquidity provider in a constant-product pool loses value relative to holding when prices move: about two percent for a one-and-a-half times move,

13
00:01:02.864 --> 00:01:09.343
about six percent for a doubling, and twenty percent for a four times move, before fees.

14
00:01:10.743 --> 00:01:13.901
Finally, write a report others can check.

15
00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:17.060
Every number cites its source or formula.

16
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.682
Observations, calculations and interpretations are labelled,

17
00:01:21.682 --> 00:01:26.458
and a limitations section names what would change the picture.

18
00:01:27.857 --> 00:01:34.273
In the course you will analyse protocols with DefiLlama data, stress-test liquidity,

19
00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:38.092
build scenarios, and write a full research report.

20
00:01:38.092 --> 00:01:43.591
A report describes evidence and uncertainty; it is not a recommendation.

21
00:01:43.591 --> 00:01:46.722
This is education, not investment advice.

